## 9. Other validation / side-effects in the flow (in execution order)

Ordered list of everything that validates or has a side-effect when `POST /api/owners` runs:

1. Deserialization + Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid`, section 2). Failure → `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (advice 7).
2. `@PreAuthorize` role check — only when security enabled (section 6).
3. `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` — MapStruct mapping. Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`, method `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (lines 59-61) ignores `id` and `pets`. Generated impl: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/annotations/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapperImpl.java`. Note: `sharesHousehold` is not mapped onto the entity (entity has no such field); it is only read from the DTO in the controller.
4. Telephone normalization + validation: `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize(...)` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/TelephoneNormalizer.java`). Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps explicit `+CC`, else assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; must be 8-15 digits after `+`. Invalid → `InvalidTelephoneException` → 400. The normalized value REPLACES the owner's telephone (side-effect, controller line 111).
5. Email normalization + validation: `EmailNormalizer.normalize(...)` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/EmailNormalizer.java`). `null` passes through; otherwise must match the email regex or `InvalidEmailException` → 400; valid values are lower-cased (side-effect, controller line 112).
6. Registration date defaulting: if null, set to `LocalDate.now()` (side-effect, controller lines 113-115).
7. Duplicate-telephone check: streams `findAllOwners()`, compares each existing owner's `toE164(telephone)` to the new normalized telephone; match → `DuplicateTelephoneException` → 409 (controller lines 116-121).
8. Duplicate-household check (skipped if `sharesHousehold == true`): normalizes lastName + address via `IdentityNormalizer` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/IdentityNormalizer.java` — trim, collapse internal whitespace, lower-case, null→""); if an existing owner matches both → `DuplicateHouseholdException` → 409 (controller lines 122-132).
9. `clinicService.createOwner(owner)` — `@Transactional`; auto-assigns `customerCode` if null via `nextCustomerCode` (extra `findAll()` count), then `ownerRepository.save` (section 3b).
10. On persist/flush, Hibernate Bean Validation enforces the ENTITY-level constraints (section 4), notably `Owner.telephone` `@Pattern ^\+[0-9]{8,15}$` and all `@NotEmpty` fields.
11. DB-level constraints (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql`, `owners` table lines 31-41): `first_name VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL`, `last_name VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL`, `address VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL`, `city VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL`, `telephone VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL`, `email VARCHAR(255)`, `registration_date DATE`, `customer_code VARCHAR(20)`. Note the DB caps `telephone` at 20 chars (DTO allows 40) and `customer_code` at 20. A violation surfaces as `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404 (advice 7). No UNIQUE constraints on the table (uniqueness of telephone/household is enforced only in the controller).
12. Response mapping: `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` computes derived fields `displayName` (`"LastName, FirstName"`) and `initials` (e.g. `"G.F."`) — see `OwnerMapper` lines 21-57. `Location` header set to `/api/owners/{id}`; returns 201 CREATED.
13. AOP monitoring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java` (`@Aspect`, `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")`) counts/times calls to `@Repository`-annotated beans. Under the ACTIVE `spring-data-jpa` profile the repository is the Spring Data interface (not `@Repository`-annotated), so as the class's own Javadoc notes, this aspect does NOT join the owner-save call by default; it would only apply under the `jpa` profile (`JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` is `@Repository`).

No emails, no external HTTP calls, no cache operations (no `@EnableCaching`/`@Cacheable`/`@CacheEvict` anywhere) occur in this flow.
